---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout class="resume">
  <hgroup>
    <h1>Carter McBride</h1>
    <p>Software Engineer · Saratoga Springs, Utah</p>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:jobs@carter.works">jobs@carter.works</a> ·
      <a href="https://carter.works">carter.works</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/carterworks">github.com/carterworks</a> ·
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thatcartermcbride/"
        >linkedin.com/in/thatcartermcbride</a
      >
    </p>
  </hgroup>

  <p>
    Web developer since 2016, now the lead contributor to Adobe’s open-source
    Web SDK. The thread through every job: make web software faster for the
    people using it and easier to ship for the people building it.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Experience</h2>

    <article>
      <h3>Software Engineer, Adobe <span>Jan 2022 – Present</span></h3>
      <p>Lehi, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Lead contributor to the Adobe Experience Platform Web SDK (<a
            href="https://github.com/adobe/alloy">adobe/alloy</a
          >), the open-source analytics and personalization library on
          enterprise sites: about 60% of the pull requests people merged in 2026.
        </li>
        <li>
          Modernized its codebase: a monorepo with automated, retry-safe
          releases, and fast, deterministic tests in place of a neglected
          end-to-end suite.
        </li>
        <li>
          Wrote the plan to take it beyond the browser as a Universal JavaScript
          SDK for Node.js too, and split out its platform-agnostic core as the
          first step.
        </li>
        <li>
          Kept it fast for visitors and the people configuring it: 9% smaller by
          retiring Internet Explorer, and settings typing lag cut from 140–209 ms
          to under 15 ms.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>
        Software Developer, ICE Mortgage Technology <span
          >Jan 2019 – Jan 2022</span
        >
      </h3>
      <p>Provo, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Improved the performance of critical-path features in software for
          mortgage lenders, championed simpler workflows for large customers,
          and mentored new hires.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>Software Engineer, Lingotek <span>May 2018 – Dec 2018</span></h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Made the main product faster to use and to build: 15% faster page
          loads by moving pages to Vue.js, and 25% faster builds on modern
          tooling.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article>
      <h3>
        Front-End Web Developer, Brigham Young University <span
          >Feb 2016 – May 2018</span
        >
      </h3>
      <p>Provo, Utah</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Built features for Learning Suite, BYU’s learning management system,
          used by thousands, with unit tests and automated setup that kept it
          reliable and onboarding quick.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://yazzy.carter.works">Yazzy</a>: reader mode for any
        web article, in Astro.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/carterworks/substack-to-epub"
          >substack-to-epub</a
        >: saves a Substack newsletter to SQLite and formats it as an EPUB, in
        Python.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://carter.works">carter.works</a>: this site, with its
        pixel-art backdrop extracted into a self-contained web components package.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <h3>
      B.S. Computer Science, Brigham Young University <span>2015 – 2019</span>
    </h3>
    <p>
      Minor in Portuguese. Third place, BYU Google Games 2017.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Skills</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Languages</dt>
      <dd>TypeScript, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Python, Go</dd>
      <dt>Web</dt>
      <dd>Web components, Astro, React, Vue.js, Node.js</dd>
      <dt>Tooling</dt>
      <dd>
        Vite, Rollup, Vitest, Playwright, pnpm, GitHub Actions, Claude Code
      </dd>
      <dt>Spoken</dt>
      <dd>English, Brazilian Portuguese</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  :global(.resume) {
    --flow-space: var(--size-sm);

    display: grid;
    gap: var(--size-md);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 1.6em;
  }

  h2 {
    border-block-end: 1px solid;
    font-size: 1em;
    margin-block-end: var(--size-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h3 {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: 1em;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  h3 span {
    font-weight: normal;
  }

  article + article {
    margin-block-start: var(--size-sm);
  }

  ul {
    padding-inline-start: 1.2em;
  }

  dl {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0 var(--size-sm);
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  @media print {
    @page {
      margin: 0.5in;
      size: letter;
    }

    :global(html) {
      color-scheme: light;
      font-size: 10pt;
    }

    :global(body) {
      background: none;
      color: #000;
      display: block;
    }

    :global(pixel-backdrop),
    :global(body > .stack > header) {
      display: none;
    }

    :global(.resume) {
      background: none;
      gap: var(--size-sm);
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
    }

    a {
      color: inherit;
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    a[href]::after {
      content: none;
    }
  }
</style>
